WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.067 --> 00:00:17.493
When the queen traveled with the king, she liked to take Glumdalclitch and me with her.

2
00:00:17.494 --> 00:00:21.375
I enjoyed traveling with them and seeing the countryside.

3
00:00:21.376 --> 00:00:26.624
I was amazed at how big Brobdingnag was compared to England.

4
00:00:26.625 --> 00:00:29.754
"I can't believe the size of your country!"

5
00:00:29.755 --> 00:00:32.443
I often exclaimed to Glumdalclitch.

6
00:00:32.444 --> 00:00:37.753
"It is five thousand kilometers wide and ten thousand kilometers long.

7
00:00:37.754 --> 00:00:41.109
England would fit into it many times over!

8
00:00:41.110 --> 00:00:45.993
I wonder why we in England have never heard of Brobdingnag."

9
00:00:45.994 --> 00:00:51.619
"The tutor said that my country is a peninsula," she reminded me.

10
00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:56.036
"That means that the sea surrounds the country on three sides.

11
00:00:56.037 --> 00:01:03.626
On the fourth side, the mountains are so high that no one has ever been able to cross them.

12
00:01:03.627 --> 00:01:09.029
The sea near Brobdingnag is full of rocks and always very rough.

13
00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:14.120
Before your ship, no other ship had ever come close to Brobdingnag.

14
00:01:14.121 --> 00:01:18.795
You are the first person from another country to come here."

15
00:01:18.796 --> 00:01:22.834
"My ship had almost run out of water," I told her.

16
00:01:22.835 --> 00:01:24.418
"We were desperate.

17
00:01:24.419 --> 00:01:28.125
That is why the sailors and I came here in the rowboat.

18
00:01:28.126 --> 00:01:31.663
We were lucky to find a little beach to land on."

19
00:01:31.664 --> 00:01:35.726
During our travels, I learned a lot about Brobdingnag.

20
00:01:35.727 --> 00:01:41.947
It contained 51 big cities, hundreds of large towns, and many villages.

21
00:01:41.948 --> 00:01:44.214
We lived in the capital city.

22
00:01:44.215 --> 00:01:48.743
A river about five kilometers wide ran through the capital.

23
00:01:48.744 --> 00:01:55.325
The palace, which was near the river, was not just one building, but dozens of buildings.

24
00:01:55.326 --> 00:02:00.606
Even the smallest one was many times bigger than the largest building in England.

25
00:02:00.607 --> 00:02:04.286
What really amazed me about the palace was the kitchen.

26
00:02:04.287 --> 00:02:07.303
Glumdalclitch and I visited it one day.

27
00:02:07.304 --> 00:02:13.421
"It looks to be almost two hundred meters high!" I exclaimed to Glumdalclitch.

28
00:02:13.422 --> 00:02:17.692
"And I've never seen pots and pans and knives this big.

29
00:02:17.693 --> 00:02:21.347
That knife there is three times as tall as I am!

30
00:02:21.348 --> 00:02:27.930
If I ever get back to England, no one will believe me when I tell them about this kitchen."

31
00:02:27.931 --> 00:02:31.047
My days in the capital were very pleasant.

32
00:02:31.048 --> 00:02:33.827
Sometimes Glumdalclitch said to me,

33
00:02:33.828 --> 00:02:37.079
"Let's go out and explore the city.

34
00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:40.162
We always see such interesting things.

35
00:02:40.163 --> 00:02:46.108
Because I lived on a farm, I am just as curious as you are about this city."

36
00:02:46.109 --> 00:02:49.512
I enjoyed exploring, so I always said,

37
00:02:49.513 --> 00:02:51.703
"That's a great idea."

38
00:02:51.704 --> 00:02:56.373
We traveled in one of the palace carriages pulled by horses.

39
00:02:56.374 --> 00:03:00.631
Glumdalclitch put me in my box and held it on her lap.

40
00:03:00.632 --> 00:03:05.511
"Look at that," she would say to me when something caught her attention.

41
00:03:05.512 --> 00:03:07.709
"Would you like a better view?

42
00:03:07.710 --> 00:03:12.191
I'll ask the driver to stop so that you can see better."

43
00:03:12.192 --> 00:03:18.104
One day the queen said, "Your bedroom box is too big for traveling.

44
00:03:18.105 --> 00:03:24.895
Glumdalclitch has trouble holding it on her lap, and I am afraid that she might drop it.

45
00:03:24.896 --> 00:03:29.165
I will tell the carpenter to make you a smaller one."

46
00:03:29.166 --> 00:03:32.625
"How kind of you," I said to her.

47
00:03:32.626 --> 00:03:35.867
"A smaller box will be much more convenient.

48
00:03:35.868 --> 00:03:42.445
My new traveling box was about three and a half meters square and three meters high.

49
00:03:42.446 --> 00:03:47.462
Three of the walls had a window with metal bars on the outside to protect me.

50
00:03:47.463 --> 00:03:55.321
Two large loops on the fourth side of my box could be used to tie the box to the waist of whoever carried it.

51
00:03:55.322 --> 00:03:58.480
"Look!" exclaimed Glumdalclitch.

52
00:03:58.481 --> 00:04:01.636
"The furniture is attached to the floor.

53
00:04:01.637 --> 00:04:04.499
It can't move around and hurt you!"

54
00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:08.504
Also, the clever carpenter had hung a hammock from the ceiling.

55
00:04:08.505 --> 00:04:13.024
"Are you comfortable?" she asked as she carried my box.

56
00:04:13.025 --> 00:04:21.166
"Very comfortable," I replied, swinging in my cozy hammock.
